{
  "slug": "codescene-codehealth",
  "name": "Codescene Codehealth",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "A Claude Code plugin that provides CodeScene Code Health analysis tools and skills for reviewing, refactoring, and safeguarding code quality.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **9 skills** and **1 MCP server**.\n\n- **Skills** (9): `configuring-codescene-mcp` (Use when the user wants to view, set, or troubleshoot CodeScene MCP configuration such as OAuth login, access…), `explaining-code-health` (Use when a user asks what Code Health means, how to interpret scores, or why Code Health matters…), `guiding-refactoring-with-code-health` (Use when refactoring unhealthy code and needing Code Health findings to choose small safe steps and verify improvement), `installing-and-activating-codescene-mcp` (Use when installing the CodeScene MCP Server binary or package, registering it in an AI assistant, or copying…), `making-the-business-case-for-code-health` (Use when a user asks for ROI, stakeholder justification, delivery impact, or defect-risk reduction from improving Code Health…), `prioritizing-technical-debt` (Use when users with a CodeScene instance ask what to improve first across a project, which hotspots matter…), `risk-based-testing-with-code-health` (Use when a user asks what to test first based on CodeScene findings, especially for high-risk hotspots or…), `routing-work-with-code-ownership` (Use when choosing reviewers, domain experts, or likely owners for a file or directory from CodeScene project data), and 1 more\n- **MCP servers** (1): `codescene`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install codescene-codehealth@claude-community` from `codescene-oss/codescene-mcp-server` (`claude-code-plugin`).",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "codex"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 9,
    "mcp": 1
  },
